"""The files the web build and its tests take from the seed, generated by the engine itself.

    python -m dgate.readiness.export <repository root>      write them
    python -m dgate.readiness.export <repository root> --check    fail if a file is out of date

  web/lib/mock/requirements.json     the catalogue, each requirement and the rules, as the API serves
                                     them: what the site shows when it is built without an API (CI)
  web/e2e/fixtures/assess-<k>.json   the API's answer for the two test profiles of the wizard e2e specs
  web/e2e/fixtures/request-<k>.json  the request body the wizard has to send for those answers

A test (tests/unit/test_readiness_export.py) runs the `--check`, so the fixtures cannot drift from the
rules: the e2e specs state verdicts that the Python engine produced from the same seed.
"""

